00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:13.129
About thirty-seven hundred kilometers southwest
of Hawaii, and thirty-seven hundred kilometers

00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:17.369
northeast of Australia, lie The Marshall Islands.

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:20.330
Getting here is not particularly easy.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:26.359
The only flights from the United States are
through Honolulu, only with United, and only

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.090
a few days of the week.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:32.969
Which helps explain why only about 6,000 people
visit each year.

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:35.510
16, a day, on average.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.430
But once you arrive, getting around is quite
easy.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.789
While the country is spread out across a thousand
islands and 29 atolls, altogether, the size

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:52.010
of Washington DC, about 40% of its 75,000
people live on the capital, Majuro.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:58.370
There are, generously, four hotels, a couple
ATMs, and one main road.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.800
No traffic lights.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.129
No street names.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:08.790
A taxi downtown costs about 50 cents, or,
across the island, at most, two US Dollars.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.910
Some may see its isolation from the rest of
the world as inconvenient.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.450
But for the people of the Marshall Islands,
that’s its charm.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.970
Life here is relaxed, care-free, and, rather
slow.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:26.650
Cars rarely move much faster than 25 miles
an hour, appointments are loosely scheduled,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.360
and Hawaiian shirts, the national dress code.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.280
In the last few years, however, the world
has been intruding.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.990
As sea levels rise, its beaches are slowly
being swallowed by the ocean.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:44.350
And, unfortunately, the Marshall Islands are
almost entirely beaches.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:51.140
Most land is barely 6-feet above sea level,
and in many areas, only 4, 500 feet wide - so

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.970
narrow you can almost always see water from
two opposite sides.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:01.890
Some years, like 2013, floods damage hundreds
of homes, schools, and stop planes from being

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.250
able to land.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:08.700
The same thing is happening around the world,
but here on small, faraway islands, the clock

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.750
is ticking, and the question of what to do,
yet unanswered.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.950
For the first time in history, countries may
totally disappear.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.090
Not politically but literally and physically.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:26.140
Where once lay a thriving, tropical paradise
community may one day be only a floating sign

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.530
explaining what once was.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:33.230
Unless, something can be done to save them.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.670
Like many islands in strategically useful
places, the Republic of The Marshall Islands

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.170
has a long history of foreign imperialism.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.570
First, by the Spanish, then the Germans, some
brief contact with the British, invaded by

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:48.000
the Japanese in World War I,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.050
And, finally, during the next war, captured
from Japan by the United States.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:58.480
It, and its neighbors now known as Palau,
the Northern Mariana Islands, and the Federated

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:04.310
States of Micronesia, were put under the administration
of the U.S. Navy as the Trust Territory of

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.819
the Pacific Islands.

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:09.201
Later, in the ’80s and ‘90s, the Islands
slowly gained their independence.

00:03:09.201 --> 00:03:15.630
The U.S. government officially recognized
its constitution, allowed it to hold elections,

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.170
and signed a Compact of Free Association.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:23.540
Today, the Marshall Islands are less than
a United States overseas territory, like Guam

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.190
or Puerto Rico, but much more than simply
a friendly foreign ally.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:30.530
Legally, an associated state.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:35.691
The islands have access to its federal agencies,
including the National Weather Service, Federal

00:03:35.691 --> 00:03:38.800
Aviation Administration, and Postal Service.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.670
The U.S. also agrees to protect and defend
the country, although it cannot declare war

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.330
on its behalf.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:52.060
This part of the United States but not really
relationship can create some… awkward situations.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:58.260
In 2015, the Iranian Navy seized and detained
a Maersk container ship traveling 12,000 kilometers

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.130
away, in the Strait of Hormuz.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:04.959
Maersk is a Danish company, and the ship,
owned by a Singapore-based operator.

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:10.250
However, for tax-avoidance and legal reasons,
it was registered, like many ships, in the

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.260
Marshall Islands.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:16.380
Which, because of its defense responsibilities,
technically obligated the U.S. Navy to respond

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:20.540
with a destroyer, although it later clarified
it won’t do so in the future.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:26.139
Besides a small coconut, breadfruit, and fishing
industry, the Marshall Islands just doesn’t

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:28.490
have that many ways to make money.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:32.460
Without many natural resources, it’s had
to resort to creative ways of bringing in

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.940
revenue, like, becoming the second most popular
ship registry in the world, after Panama.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.860
And, although sometimes lucrative, these niche
markets can make the entire economy of a small

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:46.150
nation vulnerable to the whims of foreign
actors.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:51.760
Its neighbor, Kiribati, for example, is geographically
blessed as the closest non-American soil to

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.220
the Hawaiian islands.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:58.370
So, despite having almost no infrastructure
or tourist attractions, its Tabuaeran island

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:03.370
became a regular stop for Hawaiian cruises,
who, as foreign-registered ships, are legally

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.870
required to stop, at least once, outside the
country.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:12.000
Recently, though, Norwegian Cruises introduced
American-flagged ships, rendering the detour

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.000
unnecessary.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.890
And Tabuaeran, back where it started, with
virtually no source of income.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:22.850
In a similar vein, Palau is lucky to be home
to a unique species of golden jellyfish which

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.430
draw tourists from around the world.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:30.720
Unfortunately, they too are slowly dying,
which researchers suspect is due, in part,

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.180
to rising sea temperatures.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:37.540
So, inevitably, with no other options, these
states turn to diplomacy.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:44.180
Of the 17 other UN members who recognize Taiwan
as a country, for example, nine are small,

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:45.260
island nations.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.290
It shares embassies with the Marshall Islands.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:51.740
And Taiwan’s president, at the time, was
the first head of state to officially visit

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.740
the country.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.949
The Islands also receive $78 million dollars
in U.S. foreign assistance each year, of the

00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:02.229
1.5 billion they’ve been promised from 2004
to 24.

00:06:02.229 --> 00:06:04.729
Of course, there’s no such thing as a free
lunch.

00:06:04.729 --> 00:06:10.729
And perhaps nowhere is that more apparent
than here, at the giant, concrete, American-built,

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:14.290
radioactive dome on Enewetak Atoll.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:18.639
When the U.S. assumed control of the islands
in the ‘40s, it used them as a nuclear test

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:22.590
site for some of the largest and most destructive
bombs in history.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:25.550
Including, the famous Castle Bravo.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:33.700
At 6:45 on March 1st, 1954, its mushroom cloud
could be seen 250 miles, or 400 kilometers,

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:40.880
away, eventually reaching 47 thousand feet,
or 14 kilometers, expanding at 220 miles an

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.190
hour, and leaving a 250-foot deep hole in
the ocean.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:50.790
The explosion was two and a half times stronger
than expected - 15 megatons of TNT, instead

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.330
of the predicted six.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:57.320
It instantly destroyed many of their measuring
instruments, contaminated a nearby Japanese

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.970
fishing crew, and, although inhabitants had
been evacuated beforehand, because of the

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:07.139
unexpected size of the explosion, covered
surrounding islands in a white, snow-like,

00:07:07.139 --> 00:07:08.660
radioactive powder.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.290
Children played with it, not knowing of its
cancerous effects.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:18.580
Decades later, in 1977, four thousand US soldiers
were sent to clean up the fallout.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:25.910
Over three years, they collected 73,000 cubic
meters of soil and 400 chunks of plutonium-239,

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.920
an isotope with a radioactive half-life of
24,000 years.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:35.790
It was then thrown into the crater created
by the explosion, and covered in a 328 foot,

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:40.060
or 100 meter, 18-inch thick, UFO-shaped dome.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:45.430
This was said to be only a temporary solution,
as it was not covered with a lining, meaning

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:49.800
there’s a good chance, according to the
US Energy Department, that the toxic, radioactive

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:55.310
material has already begun leaking out into
the ocean, where Marshall Islanders fish and

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.310
play.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:00.700
Today, in exchange for its payments, the US
continues to operate the Ronald Reagan Ballistic

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.620
Missile Defense Test Site.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:07.050
The US Army is one of the biggest employers
on the islands, which have a higher per-capita

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.420
enlistment rate than any state.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:13.889
And because of its proximity to the equator,
SpaceX has launched several of its rockets

00:08:13.889 --> 00:08:15.120
here in the past.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:19.810
So, while the Marshall Islands have little
leverage with the U.S., there is some hope

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:25.380
it will be forced to deal with rising sea
levels as it begins to affect military operations.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:30.920
Aerial images show six islets disappeared
between 2007 and 14 alone.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.019
Although, not all islands are equally at risk.

00:08:34.019 --> 00:08:39.149
Some, like the Maldives, are almost completely
flat, offering no place to retreat.

00:08:39.149 --> 00:08:43.360
Others, like Palau, have upland areas residents
can move too.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:48.380
Each is differently susceptible to erosion,
and some have more or less powerful waves.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:53.480
A few islands, like Tuvalu, may actually grow
as storms carry sediment, which varies with

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:55.129
seasonal trade winds.

00:08:55.129 --> 00:08:59.029
But almost everywhere on earth will be, somehow,
affected.

00:08:59.029 --> 00:09:04.589
Venice, the Everglades, Waikiki, and Alaska,
are all at risk.

00:09:04.589 --> 00:09:09.680
One small Alaskan town, The Last Frontier
of The Last Frontier, Shishmaref, has been

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.790
losing ten of its thirteen hundred feet every
year, as winter waves slam into the island

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:19.149
and the permafrost underneath it thaws, weakening
its foundation.

00:09:19.149 --> 00:09:25.839
All these islands have, essentially, three
options: Mitigate, Innovate, or Relocate.

00:09:25.839 --> 00:09:31.790
If land is disappearing, the obvious solution
is the China or Dubai approach: add more.

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:36.070
Barriers and jetties could also dampen the
blow of incoming waves.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:41.019
Unfortunately, these would likely harm marine
life, be extremely costly, and, as long as

00:09:41.019 --> 00:09:44.459
the sea continues to rise, require continual
maintenance.

00:09:44.459 --> 00:09:48.220
Better, of course, would be slowing climate
change altogether.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.660
But raising awareness is quite difficult.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:55.809
It’s geographically far-away, happening
relatively slowly, and the dynamics of wave

00:09:55.809 --> 00:10:01.149
exposure aren’t the most exciting… the
trifecta of Not Getting News Coverage.

00:10:01.149 --> 00:10:06.610
Another option is to innovate - try something,
anything, no matter how bizarre sounding,

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:08.410
to generate revenue or attention.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:13.879
In 2018, the Marshall Islands signed the Sovereign
Currency Act, which created its own national

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:15.149
cryptocurrency.

00:10:15.149 --> 00:10:19.610
If it works, the plan would give the Islands
more control over their economy, and new funds

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.129
to experiment with.

00:10:21.129 --> 00:10:26.139
Another idea, proposed by the mayor of the
Rongelap Atoll is to build “The Next Hong

00:10:26.139 --> 00:10:29.980
Kong” - a Special Administrative Region
in the middle of the Pacific.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:34.161
The idea is to use the Marshall Island’s
special relationship with the U.S. to create

00:10:34.161 --> 00:10:40.149
a tax-haven and pathway to the mainland much
like Hong Kong’s special status with China.

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:44.639
Most islands are trying a mix of these ideas,
while, also, planning for the perhaps more

00:10:44.639 --> 00:10:47.390
likely worst-case scenario: relocation.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:53.649
In 2014, Kiribati purchased a 20 square kilometer
patch of land from the Church of England in

00:10:53.649 --> 00:10:54.649
Fiji.

00:10:54.649 --> 00:10:58.129
Its president announced, “We would hope
not to put everyone on (this) one piece of

00:10:58.129 --> 00:11:02.610
land, but if it became absolutely necessary,
yes, we could do it”.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:06.990
The Marshall Islands, meanwhile, has an easier
escape: As part of its agreement with the

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:12.339
United States, its citizens are allowed to
live, work, and study on the mainland without

00:11:12.339 --> 00:11:13.339
a visa.

00:11:13.339 --> 00:11:18.740
About a third of Marshall Islanders have migrated,
many to Springdale, Arkansas, or Salem, Oregon.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.879
Although, there’s a catch.

00:11:20.879 --> 00:11:25.119
Marshallese living on the mainland are not
legally considered ‘citizens’, but also

00:11:25.119 --> 00:11:29.449
not ‘immigrants’ or ‘refugees’, they’re
“permanent non-immigrants”, which makes

00:11:29.449 --> 00:11:33.160
them ineligible for some federal services,
including Medicaid.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:38.679
And, if the Compact of Free Association is
not renewed when it ends in 2024, this door

00:11:38.679 --> 00:11:40.800
will close entirely.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:46.579
Years ago, the US government swept its radioactive
misdeeds, quite literally, under the rug.

00:11:46.579 --> 00:11:50.529
And, as sea levels rise, it seems to be doing
much the same.

00:11:50.529 --> 00:11:55.269
Ignore the problem as it grows, until, one
day, it’s too late.

00:11:55.269 --> 00:12:00.240
Today, The Marshall Islands, Tomorrow, Waikiki,
Eventually, New York.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.500
Those who’ve survived drowning report the
same pattern:

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.389
At first, an overwhelming feeling of panic.

00:12:07.389 --> 00:12:12.379
Arms flailing, legs kicking - anything, no
matter how ridiculous, to try to get the attention

00:12:12.379 --> 00:12:13.999
of the people around you.

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:19.639
Eventually, though, dread turns to tranquility
- a calmness, a dangerous complicity - a feeling

00:12:19.639 --> 00:12:22.689
that it’s too late, that nothing can be
done.

00:12:22.689 --> 00:12:25.970
The reality is it’s not too late - yet.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:31.790
The world is well into the panic stage, but,
also, at serious risk of turning into acceptance.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:37.879
It always feels like you can just hold your
breath a few more seconds, until you can’t.

00:12:37.879 --> 00:12:43.240
When the U.S. military arrived on the Marshall
Islands in 1946, asking locals to give up

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.319
their homes for what they claimed was the
good of humankind, their leader responded

00:12:47.319 --> 00:12:52.879
with the words now imprinted on the flag of
Bikini Atoll: “Everything is in the hands

00:12:52.879 --> 00:12:53.879
of God”.

00:12:53.879 --> 00:12:57.529
Now the future is in ours.

00:12:57.529 --> 00:13:02.489
Not everyone has an up-close view of rising
sea levels, but, I, for one, can really relate

00:13:02.489 --> 00:13:06.769
to the feeling of having your head underwater
- being totally overwhelmed with so much to

00:13:06.769 --> 00:13:09.079
do and so little time to do it.

00:13:09.079 --> 00:13:13.709
Recently, after watching this class on Skillshare,
I started planning pretty much every minute

00:13:13.709 --> 00:13:14.709
of my day.

00:13:14.709 --> 00:13:16.489
I used to put everything on a to-do list.

00:13:16.489 --> 00:13:20.910
But, let’s be honest, I usually ended the
week with more to do than when I started - it’s

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:24.410
a lot easier to add to the list than remember
to check it.

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:29.309
